#: sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A PREVIEW IS THE GENERAL STEP WITH A DIFFERENT ROOT (owner, 2026-09-30: \"independent of staging vs publication … just rendering\"). Process_RenderKgToCdn, entered with the tree Task_Build rendered, `branches/<slug>/` under the site root as the publication root URL, and GitHub Pages as the target, so its `gh-pages` Tool pushes. For this target the push is `keep_files: true` with a `destination_dir`, so it adds one directory beside whatever else is on the branch; it is also RETRIED once: five other workflows push to `gh-pages` without joining this one's concurrency group, and a queue does not help because GitHub CANCELS a pending job when a newer one arrives for the same group rather than queueing it. Measured 2026-09-19: three staging runs from three different branches inside 17 seconds, two cancelled. The call returns the push's status and message; the render log and the PR comment that follow are this process's own. THE PREVIEW CAP rides in the same commit (owner ruling 2026-10-02, issue #1868: \"cap the maximum number of previews (<= 10) and rotate old ones off\", amended 2026-10-04 to a SIZE budget: \"Cap by size, not count\", \"3gb\"): `staging-rotate.ts` keeps this preview plus the most recently updated others while their total fits MAX_PREVIEW_BYTES = 3 GB and removes the rest, oldest first, each with a `removed` render-log entry and its record retired into branches/_retired/. Every push attempt re-reads `gh-pages` and re-decides rather than rebasing, so a lost race never pushes a stale removal. A rotated-off preview is regenerated by the next push to its PR branch."
msgstr ""

