#: sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Build the preview from the PR's head (or, on an off-critical-path verify_pr dispatch, rebuild refs/pull/<n>/merge in full to verify an agent-built preview) and write _build-record.json: regenerate the generated docs, trim what this preview does not need, render the BPMN diagrams, then Jekyll, TypeDoc and the knowledge-graph export, with the staging banner and SEO identity claims stripped. It is a PREVIEW build (CAT_BUILD_TYPE=preview, owner 2026-11-01): only what the change reaches, and every whole-corpus index (builtAtPublish entries marked index: true, and the search index) is main's copy, put back rather than rebuilt. A branch frozen for public comment is dispatched with build_type: full instead. Skill feature-staging, section Build types. A PREVIEW REBUILDS ONLY ITS DEPENDENCY CONE (owner cards Q-CONE-1 C and Q-CONE-2 B, 2026-11-01): main's writer records say what each derive:publish writer and each step of the QA working copy READ. A writer or QA step whose recorded reads all match is not run, and main's outputs for it are put back. Every other one runs. QA is not left out of a preview, only narrowed to what the change can reach. Inside a preview's QA build, `skill:register` also leaves to derive:publish the two pages that derive:publish builds anyway and that no later QA step reads (`skills:docs` and `lsi:viz`), so they are built once."
msgstr ""

