#: sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn:97
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "On an off-critical-path verify run (verify_pr), preview-record.ts compare checks the CI rebuild's _build-record.json against the agent's record on gh-pages across every file outside the per-build metadata (staging.json, _build-record.json, .staged-at, build.yml). When every file hash matches (same = true), the agent's deployed files on branches/<slug>/ stand untouched and the deploy and render-log commits are skipped. On a normal CI build, or when the verify rebuild differs (same = false) or the merge tree moved (same = stale), the flow proceeds to push CI's build to branches/<slug>/ (guarded on verify runs so a newer preview is never overwritten)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn:154
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "ONE COMMIT for the removal and its record. A separate log push can fail on its own and leave a preview that vanished with nothing saying why — which is the exact state bean `plj1` left the branch in. `render-log.ts` refuses a `removed` entry with no reason, so this step fails loudly rather than writing a record that says an artefact went and not why."
msgstr ""

