#: sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn:31
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs all three entry points — stage, cleanup, cleanup-dispatch — as one actor because none of the work in any of them needs judgement; the one step that does, confirming a dispatch deletion, was carved out into Lane_Human rather than left here. Every path that changes `branches/` writes its render-log entry in the SAME commit as the change, because a log push that can fail on its own is exactly how a preview vanishes with nothing on the branch saying why. A FOURTH trigger starts none of them, and that is deliberate rather than an omission from this diagram. `merge_group` is declared on the workflow so it REPORTS in the merge queue — a required check that never reports on a `merge_group` event leaves every queued pull request pending forever — and all three jobs skip on it. A preview exists for the reviewers of a pull request; a queue entry has none and lives for minutes. Without the skip, `stage`'s existing guards all pass on a queue run (`github.event.action` is empty and the event is not a dispatch), so it would publish `branches/<slug>/` named after the ephemeral `gh-readonly-queue/...` ref, and nothing would ever remove it — `Start_Closed` below fires on `pull_request_target: closed`, and a queue branch is never a pull request that closes. That is the `plj1` shape arriving once per MERGE rather than once per pull request."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn:206
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Say what is going — size and file count — then remove branches/<slug>/ and append `removed` to the render log in the SAME commit, so a preview cannot vanish without a record of who dispatched it and why. The slug is a dispatch input, so the tool re-checks it by value rather than trusting the guard."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Set the preview/agent-build commit status on the PR head to pending, post the preview-build-verify notice on the PR, and exit the critical-path run so the runner is free. Off the critical path, preview-verify-sweep.yml (on staging workflow completion and every 15 minutes) waits until no Feature Staging run is active or queued, selects the oldest open PR whose head still has preview/agent-build = pending, and dispatches feature-staging.yml with verify_pr to rebuild and verify the agent's preview."
msgstr ""

